meta {
  name: List Modules by Branch Type
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/modules?branch_type=COMBINED
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  branch_type: COMBINED
}

docs {
  Public. Returns the ordered module list for one branch type as
  `{ key, label, group }` objects (key = the unified SYSTEM_MODULES key; label =
  its display name; group = the service-line group `common` | `diagnostic` |
  `radiology`, omitted for ungrouped/legacy-only modules). The `group` drives the
  grouped module picker in the branch form (a flat Common block + Diagnostic /
  Radiology accordions). The `branch_type` query param is snake_case and must
  match a key in the config constant (case-sensitive).

  ## Center-type model

  The branch form ships one branch type ("Combined") plus a Center Type selector
  that maps onto three keys: Main Center → `COMBINED`, Collection Center →
  `COLLECTION_CENTER`, Franchise → `FRANCHISE`. A Main Center offers both the
  diagnostic and radiology groups; Collection Center / Franchise offer the
  diagnostic group only (no `radiology`). The other keys (`DIAGNOSTIC`,
  `RADIOLOGY`, `OPD`, `PHARMACY`, `BLOOD_BANK`) are legacy — still resolvable for
  existing branches, but not offered in the new selector.

  `GET {{baseUrl}}/modules?branch_type=COMBINED` →

      { "success": true,
        "data": [
          { "key": "registration",   "label": "Registration",   "group": "common" },
          { "key": "finance",        "label": "Finance",        "group": "common" },
          { "key": "inventory",      "label": "Inventory",      "group": "common" },
          { "key": "sales",          "label": "Sales",          "group": "common" },
          { "key": "branch_admin",   "label": "Branch Admin",   "group": "common" },
          { "key": "business_admin", "label": "Business Admin", "group": "common" },
          { "key": "accession",      "label": "Accession",      "group": "diagnostic" },
          { "key": "lab_operations", "label": "Laboratory",     "group": "diagnostic" },
          { "key": "phlebotomist",   "label": "Phlebotomist",   "group": "diagnostic" },
          { "key": "radiology",      "label": "Radiology",      "group": "radiology" }
        ],
        "meta": { "timestamp": "..." } }

  - `COLLECTION_CENTER` / `FRANCHISE` return the same list minus the `radiology` row.
  - Unknown `branch_type` → 400 (see "Modules - Invalid Branch Type").
  - Known type with no modules → `data: []` (see "Modules - Empty List").

  This list is the **source of truth** for a User Management v2 branch assignment's
  `modules`: a user's per-branch `modules` (and `defaultModule`) must be drawn from
  this branch-type catalogue (else 422 MODULE_NOT_VALID_FOR_BRANCH_TYPE) **and** be
  enabled on the specific branch (Branches → Set Branch Modules; else 422
  MODULE_NOT_ENABLED_FOR_BRANCH). See "06 Users → User Management v2 → Create User /
  Assign Branches".
}
